---
description: Leaves, honest functions, no bool args, no wasted clones, no macros for repetition
globs: src/**/*.rs,tests/**/*.rs,docs/**/*.md
alwaysApply: true
---

Read and follow `docs/LEAVES.md` before writing or changing Rust.

Short version:

- Domain lives in `src/leaf` only. A leaf is values in, `Result<Effect, DomainError>` out.
- Leaves never do I/O: no SQLite, clock, UUID, cookies, env, sockets, or `crate::sdk` / `crate::http` / `crate::db`.
- Functions are honest. Name, arguments, and return type say what happens. No hidden side effects.
- Never pass `bool` as a function argument. Use a descriptive enum or two functions.
- Return a specific `DomainError`. Do not reuse `NotGovernor` for a different kind of person.
- Do not clone a collection to walk it again. Iterate, move, or borrow (`NeedSight`).
- Loops live in their own named function. Page bodies compose those functions.
- Do not write macros to hide repetition (HTTP gates, write dispatch, status strings). Extract a function, an enum, or a trait after a second identical use.
- HTTP loads values, calls a leaf, commits the effect. It does not decide membership, visibility, or endorsements.

`us_clean_01`, `us_perf_01`, and `us_leaf_01` in `src/style.rs` enforce this. Run `cargo test style` after changing `src/`.
